    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by **Brice Turang** (62.96) and **Corbin Carroll** (66.89). **Brice Turang** is our strongest play relative to expectation; he benefits significantly from a top-third lineup position and a favorable matchup against a middling lefty in M. P\u00e9rez. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains a core engine for our stolen base targets; despite the platoon disadvantage against Prielipp, his raw ceiling and placement in the three-hole provide the necessary floor to lead the outfield. **Tyler Soderstrom** also surges to a 65.47 rating, bolstered by a significant park factor and a solid righty-on-righty platoon profile against Soriano, making him a high-efficiency play today.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision was bypassing **Cole Young** (40.23) for the final utility spot. While **Cole Young** provides peripheral utility, his low park-adjusted projection and the inherent defensive risk of facing Suarez kept him on the bench in favor of **Kyle Karros** (48.47). **Kyle Karros** earns the nod primarily due to the +14% park factor, which mitigates the negative impact of his nine-hole placement. We are monitoring the status of **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland** closely; both are currently projected in the #8 and #9 spots respectively against the shaky Trey Gibson (5.63 xERA). While the wind-out conditions at the park provide a meaningful boost to their profiles, any further demotion in their batting order could necessitate a late-inning pivot. We proceed with caution against Misiorowski, who represents the toughest test of the day for **Austin Riley**, as his elite arm (2.70 xERA) threatens to suppress the offensive output of our 3B slot.",
